### SupplyChain Passport — manual API tests
### Open in VS Code with the "REST Client" extension and click "Send Request" above each block.

@api = http://localhost:4000/api

### Health check
GET {{api}}/health

### List products
GET {{api}}/products

### Get one product
GET {{api}}/products/1

### Get a product that doesn't exist  → 404
GET {{api}}/products/999

### AT-01: create a valid product  → 201
POST {{api}}/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test Glove",
  "sku": "tg-2001",
  "category": "Protective Gloves",
  "description": "A product created while testing the API.",
  "primary_material": "Cotton",
  "manufacture_country": "Sri Lanka",
  "image_url": ""
}

### AT-02: duplicate SKU  → 422
POST {{api}}/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Copy of EcoGrip",
  "sku": "EGP-1001",
  "category": "Protective Gloves",
  "description": "Should be rejected.",
  "primary_material": "Nitrile",
  "manufacture_country": "Sri Lanka"
}

### Missing required fields  → 422 with an error per field
POST {{api}}/products
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Update a product (replace the id with the one from the create response)  → 200
PUT {{api}}/products/2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test Glove v2",
  "sku": "TG-2001",
  "category": "Protective Gloves",
  "description": "Updated description.",
  "primary_material": "Cotton",
  "manufacture_country": "Sri Lanka",
  "image_url": "https://example.com/glove.png"
}

### Delete a product  → 204
DELETE {{api}}/products/2

### ============================================================
### Suppliers
### ============================================================

### List suppliers (each one includes stage_count)  → 200
GET {{api}}/suppliers

### Create a supplier  → 201
POST {{api}}/suppliers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test Supplier",
  "country": "Sri Lanka",
  "location": "Colombo",
  "contact": "test@example.com"
}

### Missing required fields  → 422 with an error for name and country
POST {{api}}/suppliers
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Update a supplier (replace the id with the one from the create response)  → 200
PUT {{api}}/suppliers/5
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test Supplier v2",
  "country": "Sri Lanka",
  "location": "",
  "contact": "updated@example.com"
}

### Delete an unused supplier (use the id from the create response)  → 204
DELETE {{api}}/suppliers/5

### Delete a supplier used in a stage (pick an id with stage_count > 0 from the list)  → 409
DELETE {{api}}/suppliers/1

### Get a supplier that doesn't exist  → 404
GET {{api}}/suppliers/999

### ===== Certifications =====
### (Product id 1 = EcoGrip Pro after `npm run db:reset`. Check with GET {{api}}/products if unsure.)

### Test 1 — AT-04: past expiry → status "Expired"
POST {{api}}/products/1/certifications
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Old Audit (demo record)",
  "issuer": "Example Audit Group",
  "certificate_number": "DEMO-OLD-010",
  "issued_at": "2020-01-01",
  "expires_at": "2021-01-01"
}

### Test 2 — AT-05: future issue date → status "Not yet valid"
POST {{api}}/products/1/certifications
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Planned Certificate (demo record)",
  "issuer": "Example Certification Body",
  "certificate_number": "DEMO-PLAN-011",
  "issued_at": "2030-01-01",
  "expires_at": ""
}

### Test 3 — no expiry date → status "No expiry provided"
POST {{api}}/products/1/certifications
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Supplier Declaration (demo record)",
  "issuer": "GreenFibre Ltd",
  "certificate_number": "DEMO-DECL-012",
  "issued_at": "2026-01-01"
}

### Test 4 — AT-06: expiry before issue → 422
POST {{api}}/products/1/certifications
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Broken Dates",
  "issuer": "X",
  "certificate_number": "X-1",
  "issued_at": "2026-05-01",
  "expires_at": "2026-01-01"
}

### Test 5 — impossible date → 422
POST {{api}}/products/1/certifications
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Bad Date",
  "issuer": "X",
  "certificate_number": "X-2",
  "issued_at": "2026-02-30"
}

### Test 6 — product that doesn't exist → 404
POST {{api}}/products/999/certifications
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Orphan",
  "issuer": "X",
  "certificate_number": "X-3",
  "issued_at": "2026-01-01"
}

### Test 7 — update (REPLACE 4 with the id from Test 1) → 200, status recalculated
PUT {{api}}/certifications/4
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Old Audit (demo record)",
  "issuer": "Example Audit Group",
  "certificate_number": "DEMO-OLD-010",
  "issued_at": "2020-01-01",
  "expires_at": "2030-01-01"
}

### Test 8 — delete (REPLACE 4 with the id from Test 1) → 204; send again → 404
DELETE {{api}}/certifications/4

### ===== Stages =====
### After `npm run db:reset`: product 1 = EcoGrip Pro, stages 1–4, suppliers 1–4.

### Test 1 — full product detail (stages + certificates)
GET {{api}}/products/1

### Test 2 — add a stage → goes to the end (position 5)
POST {{api}}/products/1/stages
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "stage_name": "Quality inspection",
  "supplier_id": "3"
}

### Test 3 — missing name and supplier → 422
POST {{api}}/products/1/stages
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "stage_name": "",
  "supplier_id": ""
}

### Test 4 — supplier that doesn't exist → 422
POST {{api}}/products/1/stages
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "stage_name": "Packing",
  "supplier_id": 999
}

### Test 5 — reorder: move "Quality inspection" (id 5) before "Distribution" (id 4)
PUT {{api}}/products/1/stages/order
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "stage_ids": [1, 2, 3, 5, 4]
}

### Test 6 — invalid reorder: a stage missing → 422
PUT {{api}}/products/1/stages/order
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "stage_ids": [1, 2, 3]
}

### Test 7 — invalid reorder: duplicate id → 422
PUT {{api}}/products/1/stages/order
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "stage_ids": [1, 1, 2, 3, 4]
}

### Test 8 — edit a stage's name (Scenario F: correcting the journey)
PUT {{api}}/stages/2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "stage_name": "Fabric weaving",
  "supplier_id": 2
}

### Test 9 — delete stage 5 → the gap closes (send twice: second → 404)
DELETE {{api}}/stages/5

### Test 10 — full reversal (the hardest case for the unique constraint)
PUT {{api}}/products/1/stages/order
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "stage_ids": [4, 3, 2, 1]
}

### Test 11 — back to the original order
PUT {{api}}/products/1/stages/order
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "stage_ids": [1, 2, 3, 4]
}

### ===== Passport =====
### Run in order after `npm run db:reset`.

### Step 1 — AT-07: not published yet → 404
GET {{api}}/public/passports/EGP-1001

### Step 2 — AT-11: unknown SKU → same 404
GET {{api}}/public/passports/NOPE-0000

### Step 3 — admin preview (draft) → is_published: false
GET {{api}}/products/1/passport-preview

### Step 4 — AT-08: publish
POST {{api}}/products/1/publish

### Step 5 — public passport now works (no login)
GET {{api}}/public/passports/EGP-1001

### Step 6 — AT-09 part 1: edit the product after publishing
PUT {{api}}/products/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "EcoGrip Pro (2nd edition)",
  "sku": "EGP-1001",
  "category": "Protective Gloves",
  "description": "Reusable protective work glove. Updated description.",
  "primary_material": "Recycled polyester and nitrile",
  "manufacture_country": "Sri Lanka"
}

### Step 7 — AT-09 part 2 (Scenario F): correct a supplier's name
PUT {{api}}/suppliers/2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "LankaTex Mills (Pvt) Ltd",
  "country": "Sri Lanka",
  "location": "Gampaha"
}

### Step 8 — AT-09 check: public passport is UNCHANGED
GET {{api}}/public/passports/EGP-1001

### Step 9 — preview shows the new data + has_unpublished_changes: true
GET {{api}}/products/1/passport-preview

### Step 10 — AT-10: republish
POST {{api}}/products/1/publish

### Step 11 — AT-10 check: public passport now shows the changes
GET {{api}}/public/passports/EGP-1001

### Step 12 — product list shows published_at
GET {{api}}/products